Z||000040||TooManyFieros||10-02-2001||11:28 AM||||Any of the places that you mentioned. Since we are getting late in the season, call around. The kit is what you would expect it to be called - A R-134A conversion kit. It includes 1 can of oil, 3 cans of 134 and a hose to put it in the car plus adapters for R-134A to R-12.  Jim  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haagster:<BR><B> Where can I get a conversion kit?  Pep Boys, Advance Auto Parts, or the like?  What kit?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000041||skitime||10-02-2001||12:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B> Where is the diner(street address)...gotta map it see if I feel like getting up at 4am?!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>For those joining us for breakfast and the cruise to the Gilbert's Tech Session but need directions, go to the web site <A HREF="http://www.mapquest.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mapquest.com</A>   Enter the address of the Silk City Diner which is 1640 North Reading Road, Stevens PA 17578.  You can get driving directions to the diner by clicking on the DRIVING DIRECTION button in the upper left corner.  Let me know if you plan to be at breakfast and how many will be with you so I can make resevations.<P><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
